{"step_index":440,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T12:53:04Z","content":"A comprehensive technical report has been compiled and saved to the artifact:\n👉 [centreon-map-chain-report.md](file:///home/koby/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/6237460b-4163-4167-a26e-b8194f657433/centreon-map-chain-report.md)\n\n---\n\n### Key Takeaways\n\n1. **Root Cause of the UI Test Failure**:\n   * Network, routing, and HTTP reverse proxy layers are **fully operational** (CLI `curl -k` receives `401 Unauthorized` directly from Centreon Map's Tomcat engine).\n   * The Centreon Web UI button (*\"Test connection to server\"*) fails because its internal PHP cURL function enforces strict SSL hostname verification (`CURLOPT_SSL_VERIFYPEER = true`). The certificate currently served on port `9443` only covers `extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` and lacks `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` as a Subject Alternative Name (SAN).\n\n2. **Configurations Applied & Why**:\n   * **[`/etc/nginx/sites-available/02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf`](file:///etc/nginx/sites-available/02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf)** (`172.30.198.33`):\n     * Switched upstream to `https://172.30.198.50:9443;` with `proxy_ssl_verify off;` (resolves initial 502 Bad Gateway).\n     * Added root redirect `/` $\\rightarrow$ `/centreon-map/` (prevents Tomcat 404s).\n     * Preserved headers (`Host $http_host;`, `X-Forwarded-Port 9443;`) so internal Tomcat redirects retain port `9443`.\n   * **[`/etc/network/interfaces.d/lo-alias`](file:///etc/network/interfaces.d/lo-alias)** (`172.30.198.33`):\n     * Bound `109.62.64.18/32` to loopback (`lo:1`) to ensure local packet acceptance for the VIP.\n   * **[`/etc/hosts`](file:///etc/hosts)** (`172.30.198.49`):\n     * Added `172.30.198.33 map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` to route internal backend requests directly to the reverse proxy, bypassing the lack of firewall Hairpin NAT.\n\n---\n\n### Single Action Needed to Complete Validation\n\nExpand the Let's Encrypt certificate on [`th2-revproxyp-fe1`](file:///etc/nginx/sites-available/02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf) to include the `map.*` SAN:\n\n```bash\nsudo certbot certonly --cert-name extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr \\\n  --expand -d extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr,map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr\nsudo systemctl reload nginx\n```\n\nOnce reloaded, re-running the test button in Centreon Web will validate with a green success status."}
