{"step_index":444,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T12:59:43Z","content":"Using a **dedicated Nginx configuration file** and a **dedicated TLS certificate** for `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` is not only completely valid, but **architecturally cleaner and best-practice** for enterprise environments.\n\n---\n\n### Key Advantages of This Approach\n\n1. **Separation of Concerns (Modularity)**:\n   * [`02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf`](file:///etc/nginx/sites-available/02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf) handles strictly **Centreon Web** (`:443`) and LoRaWAN (`:8443`).\n   * A new [`03-map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf`](file:///etc/nginx/sites-available/03-map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf) handles strictly **Centreon Map** (`:9443`).\n   * Modifications, restarts, or maintenance on Map will never impact Centreon Web availability.\n\n2. **Independent Certificate Lifecycles**:\n   * If one domain encounters an ACME renewal issue (e.g. temporary DNS glitch or challenge timeout), the other certificate continues renewing independently without risk to the primary portal.\n\n3. **Isolated Logging & Tuning**:\n   * Centreon Map uses high-frequency API calls and long-lived WebSocket connections. A dedicated vhost allows isolated logs:\n     * `/var/log/nginx/centreon-map_access.log`\n     * `/var/log/nginx/centreon-map_error.log`\n   * Timeouts (`proxy_read_timeout 3600s;` for WebSockets) and ModSecurity exclusions can be tuned specifically for Map without weakening Centreon Web's security profile.\n\n---\n\n### What Implementation Looks Like\n\n#### 1. Issue the Dedicated Certificate\nRun Certbot for the subdomain only:\n```bash\nsudo certbot certonly --cert-name map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr \\\n  -d map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr\n```\n*(Files created in `/etc/letsencrypt/live/map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr/`)*\n\n#### 2. Create the Dedicated Vhost\nCreate [`/etc/nginx/sites-available/03-map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf`](file:///etc/nginx/sites-available/03-map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf):\n\n```nginx\nserver {\n    listen 9443 ssl http2 reuseport;\n    server_name map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr 109.62.64.18;\n\n    # Dedicated SSL Certificate\n    ssl_certificate /etc/letsencrypt/live/map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr/fullchain.pem;\n    ssl_certificate_key /etc/letsencrypt/live/map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr/privkey.pem;\n    ssl_trusted_certificate /etc/letsencrypt/live/map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr/chain.pem;\n\n    # Dedicated Logs\n    access_log /var/log/nginx/map.extranetclient_access.log combined;\n    error_log  /var/log/nginx/map.extranetclient_error.log warn;\n\n    # Root redirect to Map app\n    location = / {\n        return 301 /centreon-map/;\n    }\n\n    location / {\n        proxy_pass https://172.30.198.50:9443;\n        proxy_ssl_verify off;\n\n        proxy_set_header Host $http_host;\n        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;\n        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;\n        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto https;\n        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Port 9443;\n\n        # WebSocket support\n        proxy_http_version 1.1;\n        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;\n        proxy_set_header Connection $connection_upgrade;\n        proxy_read_timeout 3600s;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n#### 3. Clean up [`02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf`](file:///etc/nginx/sites-available/02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf)\n* Remove the `server { listen 9443 ... }` block from `02-extranetclient...conf` so port `9443` is exclusively managed by the new file.\n\n#### 4. Enable & Reload\n```bash\nsudo ln -s /etc/nginx/sites-available/03-map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/\nsudo nginx -t && sudo systemctl reload nginx\n```\n\n---\n\n### Comparison Summary\n\n| Metric | Multi-Domain SAN (Single Cert & File) | Separate Cert & Dedicated File (Recommended) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Effort** | Fast (1 command, no new files) | A few extra minutes to create file & symlink |\n| **Modularity** | Centreon Web and Map tightly coupled | **Fully decoupled & clean** |\n| **Maintenance** | Re-expanding if subdomains change | **Independent per-service lifecycle** |\n| **Troubleshooting** | Shared access/error logs | **Dedicated Map access & error logs** |","thinking":"**Evaluating Separate Proxy Configuration**\n\nConsidering using a dedicated Nginx configuration for the specific subdomain. This would enable applying a distinct TLS certificate specifically for `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr`. The separation allows for tailored directives and security settings, preventing potential conflicts with the main reverse proxy setup. Verify that the correct Certbot command is employed to generate this specific certificate.\n\n\n**Analyzing Proposed Nginx Configuration**\n\nThe proposed setup offers modularity with dedicated configuration files for different services, such as Centreon Web and Map. Independent certificate management is also a significant advantage, isolating certificate renewals and preventing disruptions. Separating access control and logging will provide enhanced security and easier troubleshooting.\n\nThis approach ensures service independence, simplifying maintenance and reducing the risk of a single component's failure affecting the entire system. Considering these aspects, the proposed architecture offers improved robustness and maintainability.\n\n\n"}
